{"name":"Rockweed","hex":"#443735","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rockweed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ascophyllum nodosum, a seaweed also known as knotted wrack.","Fucus vesiculosus, a similar seaweed also known as bladderwrack."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rockweed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ascophyllum","blocks":[{"text":"Ascophyllum nodosum is a large, common cold water seaweed or brown alga (Phaeophyceae) in the family Fucaceae. Its common names include knotted wrack, egg wrack, feamainn bhuí, rockweed, knotted kelp and Norwegian kelp. It grows only in the northern Atlantic Ocean, along the north-western coast of Europe including east Greenland and the north-eastern coast of North America. Its range further south of these latitudes is limited by warmer ocean waters. It dominates the intertidal zone. Ascophyllum nodosum has been used numerous times in scientific research and has even been found to benefit humans through consumption."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Ascophyllum_nodosum.jpg/330px-Ascophyllum_nodosum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ascophyllum"},{"title":"Fucus distichus","blocks":[{"text":"Fucus distichus or rockweed is a species of brown alga in the family Fucaceae to be found in the intertidal zones of rocky seashores in the Northern Hemisphere, mostly in rock pools."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Fucusdistichus.jpg/330px-Fucusdistichus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fucus_distichus"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Ascophyllum_nodosum_natural_range.jpg/500px-Ascophyllum_nodosum_natural_range.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Ascophyllum_nodosum_natural_range.jpg/500px-Ascophyllum_nodosum_natural_range.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAscophyllum_nodosum_natural_range.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Ascophyllum_nodosum_Trefdraeth_stipe.jpg/500px-Ascophyllum_nodosum_Trefdraeth_stipe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Ascophyllum_nodosum_Trefdraeth_stipe.jpg/1280px-Ascophyllum_nodosum_Trefdraeth_stipe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Ascophyllum_nodosum_Trefdraeth_stipe.jpg/500px-Ascophyllum_nodosum_Trefdraeth_stipe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Contrast between darker colored shoots and lighter colored fronds","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAscophyllum_nodosum_Trefdraeth_stipe.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Vertebrata_lanosa_on_Ascophyllum_nodosum.jpg/500px-Vertebrata_lanosa_on_Ascophyllum_nodosum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Vertebrata_lanosa_on_Ascophyllum_nodosum.jpg/1280px-Vertebrata_lanosa_on_Ascophyllum_nodosum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Vertebrata_lanosa_on_Ascophyllum_nodosum.jpg/500px-Vertebrata_lanosa_on_Ascophyllum_nodosum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Epiphytic red algae on knotted wrack at Roscoff, France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVertebrata_lanosa_on_Ascophyllum_nodosum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki